module nfkbLiveImagingDetection
module baggingClassifierDetection
module miR146aExpressionDetection
module crossToleranceDetection

manifest Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
manifest Fibronectin
manifest DMEM_CompleteMedia
manifest UltrapureLPS_100ngmL
manifest UltrapureLPS_33ngmL
manifest UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
manifest Pam3CSK4_40ngmL
manifest Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
manifest Pam3CSK4_4p4ngmL
manifest TrizolReagent
manifest snoRNA234_Control
manifest TaqMan_miR146a_Probe
manifest PBS_Wash

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Cellular Decision Making by Non-Integrative Processing
// of TLR Inputs
// Kellogg, Tian, Etzrodt, Tay - Cell Reports 19, 125-135 (2017)
// DOI: http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2017.03.027
//
// Protocol: Automated microfluidic single-cell live imaging of
// NF-kB dynamics in mouse 3T3 fibroblasts (p65-DsRed) under
// combinatorial TLR2/TLR4 co-stimulation (LPS x PAM dose matrix),
// bagging classifier-based response classification, sequential
// cross-tolerance stimulation, and miR-146a TaqMan qPCR validation.
//
// BIOLOGICAL SCOPE:
//   TLR4 agonist: Ultrapure LPS (Invivogen) -- activates TLR4
//     exclusively (Fujihara et al., 2003; Lee et al., 2009).
//   TLR2 agonist: Pam3CSK4 (PAM, Invivogen) -- synthetic
//     triacylated lipopeptide, activates TLR2 via endosomal
//     processing (Brandt et al., 2013; Stack et al., 2014).
//   Cell line: p65^(-/-) mouse 3T3 fibroblasts re-expressing
//     p65-DsRed under endogenous 1.5 kb p65 promoter; H2B-GFP
//     nuclear marker for automated tracking (Tay et al., 2010).
//
// MICROFLUIDIC PLATFORM:
//   Chambers: 1.12 mm x 0.9 mm x 0.040 mm; ~100 cells/chamber.
//   Fibronectin pre-treatment for cell adhesion.
//   Seeding density: 200 cells/chamber. 1-day pre-culture to
//   80% confluence with periodic media replenishment.
//   Stimuli diluted in DMEM equilibrated to 5% CO2; delivered
//   as step increase (chamber media exchange). All nine LPS-PAM
//   dose combinations run in parallel on a single chip.
//   Stimulations applied in duplicate chambers per condition.
//   Post-stimulation: chambers sealed; imaged every 5-6 min.
//
// IMAGING AND ANALYSIS:
//   Leica DMI6000B widefield microscope, 20x, Retiga-SRV CCD.
//   DsRed (Y3 filter) and GFP (L5 filter) channels acquired.
//   NF-kB activation = mean nuclear DsRed / mean cytoplasm DsRed.
//   CellProfiler + custom MATLAB: automated cell tracking and
//   NF-kB quantification. Peak detection via MATLAB mspeaks.
//
// NOTE ON `mix` ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` in this protocol represents the microfluidic media
//   exchange / stimulus delivery step (chamber perfusion), not
//   pipette mixing. Stimulus is delivered as a step increase in
//   chamber concentration by flushing stimulus-containing DMEM.
//   There is no droplet-level DMF merging.
//
// NOTE ON DOSE MANIFESTS:
//   Each LPS and PAM concentration is encoded as a separate
//   manifest reflecting the distinct vial preparations used in
//   the paper (LPS/PAM diluted in DMEM in separate vials,
//   pressured with 5% CO2, kept on ice before delivery).
//   This avoids the need for on-chip serial dilution, which is
//   not described in the paper's experimental procedure.
//
// NOTE ON SEQUENTIAL STIMULATION (BB6/BB7):
//   Two sequential schemes are tested:
//     Scheme A: LPS 11 ng/mL first -> PAM 13.3 ng/mL at +2 hr.
//     Scheme B: PAM 13.3 ng/mL first -> LPS 100 ng/mL at +4 hr.
//   Both probe TLR cross-tolerance mediated by miR-146a / A20 /
//   IkB negative feedback (Fig. 5, paper).
//   crossTolSignal abstracts the dual-response QC gate:
//     Scheme A result: 53% cells LPS-only, 30% PAM-only, 17% both.
//     Scheme B result: 84% cells PAM-only, 16% both (full block).
//   Signal > 0 encodes the expected cross-tolerance outcome
//   (majority of pre-stimulated cells refractory to 2nd stimulus).
//
// NOTE ON miRNA QPCRvalidation (BB8 onward):
//   Bulk RNA was isolated from cells stimulated with 10 ng/mL LPS
//   or 10 ng/mL PAM (separate conditions, not co-stimulation).
//   miR-146a induced by both; LPS onset ~1 hr, PAM onset ~2 hr;
//   sustained high expression for several hours (Fig. 2C).
//   `detect miR146aExpressionDetection` abstracts the TaqMan
//   real-time PCR assay (Applied Biosystems). Expression
//   normalised to snoRNA234 endogenous control.
//   miR146aSignal > 0 encodes detection of sustained induction.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                  -- device prep; cell seeding;
//                                 9 x LPS-PAM co-stimulation matrix
//   BB2  classifyPass          -- classifySignal > 0: predominantly
//                                 LPS-like or PAM-like (non-integrative);
//                                 dispose co-stim droplets; proceed
//   BB3  classifyFail          -- classifySignal <= 0: mixed/uncertain
//                                 response dominant; drain
//   BB4  classifyJoin          -- join: sequential cross-tolerance arm
//   BB5  seqSchemeA            -- Scheme A: LPS first -> PAM at +2 hr
//   BB5a seqSchemeA_stimulate  -- deliver second stimulus (PAM)
//   BB6  seqSchemeB            -- Scheme B: PAM first -> LPS at +4 hr
//   BB6a seqSchemeB_stimulate  -- deliver second stimulus (LPS)
//   BB7  crossTolPass          -- crossTolSignal > 0: cross-tolerance
//                                 confirmed; dispose; proceed to miRNA
//   BB8  crossTolFail          -- crossTolSignal <= 0: no cross-tol; drain
//   BB9  crossTolJoin          -- join: miR-146a validation arm
//   BB10 miR146aPass           -- miR146aSignal > 0: sustained induction
//                                 confirmed; dispose
//   BB11 miR146aFail           -- miR146aSignal <= 0: no induction; drain
//   BB12 finalCleanup          -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================


// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// Device preparation, cell seeding, and 9-condition
// LPS x PAM co-stimulation matrix.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Fibronectin coating of microfluidic chambers.
//   Chambers coated with fibronectin to promote 3T3 cell
//   adhesion. Coating applied before cell loading and allowed
//   to adsorb to PDMS surface. PBS wash removes excess.
//   `mix` abstracts the chamber perfusion coating step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinCoat = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
pbsWash1        = dispense 1 units of PBS_Wash
coatedChamber   = mix fibronectinCoat with pbsWash1 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Cell seeding and pre-culture.
//   Mouse 3T3 p65-DsRed cells seeded at 200 cells/chamber.
//   Standard culture: 37 C, 5% CO2. Cells grow for 1 day
//   with periodic media replenishment to ~80% confluence.
//   `heat` models the 24 h incubator pre-culture step.
//   NOTE: 24 h = 1440 min (BioScript supports min only, not h).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cells          = dispense 1 units of Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
mediaPreCulture = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
seededChamber  = mix cells with coatedChamber for 2s

heat seededChamber at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Replace media with fresh DMEM before stimulation.
//   Media replenishment step to remove conditioned media and
//   establish a baseline before stimulus delivery.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedia     = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
baselineChamber = mix seededChamber with freshMedia for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4a: Prepare and deliver co-stimulation condition 1
//   LPS 100 ng/mL + PAM 40 ng/mL (high-high dose).
//   Stimulus vials pre-equilibrated to 5% CO2 and kept on ice.
//   Media exchange produces a step increase in concentration.
//   Live imaging begins immediately after stimulus delivery.
//   Chambers sealed; 5-6 min imaging intervals for 480 min.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the microfluidic chamber perfusion
//   and media exchange event, not pipette mixing.
//   Duplicate chamber (cond1b) run in parallel on same chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps100         = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_100ngmL
pam40          = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_40ngmL
stimulusCond1  = mix lps100 with pam40 for 5s
cond1a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond1 for 480m
cond1b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond1 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4b: Condition 2 -- LPS 100 ng/mL + PAM 13.3 ng/mL
//   (high LPS, mid PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps100_c2      = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_100ngmL
pam13p3        = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
stimulusCond2  = mix lps100_c2 with pam13p3 for 5s
cond2a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond2 for 480m
cond2b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond2 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4c: Condition 3 -- LPS 100 ng/mL + PAM 4.4 ng/mL
//   (high LPS, low PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps100_c3      = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_100ngmL
pam4p4         = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_4p4ngmL
stimulusCond3  = mix lps100_c3 with pam4p4 for 5s
cond3a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond3 for 480m
cond3b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond3 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4d: Condition 4 -- LPS 33 ng/mL + PAM 40 ng/mL
//   (mid LPS, high PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps33          = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_33ngmL
pam40_c4       = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_40ngmL
stimulusCond4  = mix lps33 with pam40_c4 for 5s
cond4a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond4 for 480m
cond4b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond4 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4e: Condition 5 -- LPS 33 ng/mL + PAM 13.3 ng/mL
//   (mid LPS, mid PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps33_c5       = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_33ngmL
pam13p3_c5     = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
stimulusCond5  = mix lps33_c5 with pam13p3_c5 for 5s
cond5a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond5 for 480m
cond5b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond5 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4f: Condition 6 -- LPS 33 ng/mL + PAM 4.4 ng/mL
//   (mid LPS, low PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps33_c6       = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_33ngmL
pam4p4_c6      = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_4p4ngmL
stimulusCond6  = mix lps33_c6 with pam4p4_c6 for 5s
cond6a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond6 for 480m
cond6b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond6 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4g: Condition 7 -- LPS 11 ng/mL + PAM 40 ng/mL
//   (low LPS, high PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps11          = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
pam40_c7       = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_40ngmL
stimulusCond7  = mix lps11 with pam40_c7 for 5s
cond7a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond7 for 480m
cond7b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond7 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4h: Condition 8 -- LPS 11 ng/mL + PAM 13.3 ng/mL
//   (low LPS, mid PAM).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps11_c8       = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
pam13p3_c8     = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
stimulusCond8  = mix lps11_c8 with pam13p3_c8 for 5s
cond8a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond8 for 480m
cond8b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond8 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4i: Condition 9 -- LPS 11 ng/mL + PAM 4.4 ng/mL
//   (low LPS, low PAM). Primary condition for mechanistic
//   analysis: most distinct LPS-like vs PAM-like dynamics.
//   Bagging classifier trained on individual LPS/PAM responses
//   applied to classify each cell as LPS-like, PAM-like, or
//   uncertain. Fig. 4B upper-left panel. ~15% mixed/uncertain.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lps11_c9       = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
pam4p4_c9      = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_4p4ngmL
stimulusCond9  = mix lps11_c9 with pam4p4_c9 for 5s
cond9a         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond9 for 480m
cond9b         = mix baselineChamber with stimulusCond9 for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: NF-kB live imaging and bagging classifier detection.
//   nfkbLiveImagingDetection: abstracts CellProfiler/MATLAB
//     automated tracking and DsRed nuclear/cytoplasm ratio
//     quantification over 480 min at 5-6 min intervals.
//   baggingClassifierDetection: abstracts the ensemble of N=50
//     decision-tree classifiers (n=0.6 majority vote threshold)
//     trained on single-stimulus LPS and PAM trajectories.
//     Outputs LPS-like (> n fraction), PAM-like (> n fraction),
//     or uncertain (neither fraction reaches n).
//     QC gate here uses classifySignal > 0 to encode the
//     population-level finding that non-integrative processing
//     dominates (>80% LPS-like or PAM-like; <15-20% uncertain).
//   Detection is run on the primary mechanistic condition (cond9a)
//   as the representative for the classifier QC gate. All nine
//   conditions are imaged in parallel (single chip), but only
//   cond9a drives the downstream CFG branch.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nfkbSignal     = detect nfkbLiveImagingDetection on cond9a for 480m
classifySignal = detect baggingClassifierDetection on nfkbSignal for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Classifier QC gate
// Pass (BB2): classifySignal > 0 -> non-integrative processing
//             confirmed; majority of cells are LPS-like or
//             PAM-like, not mixed; dispose co-stim chamber
//             and proceed to sequential stimulation arm (BB4).
// Fail (BB3): classifySignal <= 0 -> mixed/uncertain responses
//             dominate (integrative processing); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (classifyJoin).
// ============================================================

if (classifySignal > 0) {
    dispose cond1a
    dispose cond1b
    dispose cond2a
    dispose cond2b
    dispose cond3a
    dispose cond3b
    dispose cond4a
    dispose cond4b
    dispose cond5a
    dispose cond5b
    dispose cond6a
    dispose cond6b
    dispose cond7a
    dispose cond7b
    dispose cond8a
    dispose cond8b
    dispose cond9b
} else {
    drain cond1a
    drain cond1b
    drain cond2a
    drain cond2b
    drain cond3a
    drain cond3b
    drain cond4a
    drain cond4b
    drain cond5a
    drain cond5b
    drain cond6a
    drain cond6b
    drain cond7a
    drain cond7b
    drain cond8a
    drain cond8b
    drain cond9b
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: classifyJoin
// Dispose classifier and imaging QC signal droplets.
// Control falls into the sequential cross-tolerance arm (BB5).
// ============================================================

dispose classifySignal
dispose nfkbSignal

// ============================================================
// BB5: seqSchemeA
// Sequential stimulation Scheme A: LPS 11 ng/mL delivered
// first (t=0); PAM 13.3 ng/mL delivered to the SAME cells
// at t=2 hr (120 min) later.
//
// Fresh 3T3 p65-DsRed cells are seeded and pre-cultured in a
// new chamber (parallel chip run). LPS 11 ng/mL is delivered
// as the first stimulus. `heat` at 37 C for 120 min models
// the 2-hour interval before second stimulus delivery.
// Incubation: 5% CO2, 37 C, sealed chamber. Imaging continuous.
//
// Paper result (Fig. 5C): 53% of cells responded to LPS only;
// 17% responded to both; 30% responded to PAM only (LPS-
// refractory cells caught by PAM at 2 hr). Only 17% double-
// responders indicate rapid negative feedback (IkB, A20,
// miR-146a) is sufficient to suppress subsequent PAM response
// in most LPS-activated cells.
// ============================================================

// BB5a: Cell prep for sequential scheme A
cellsSeqA       = dispense 1 units of Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
fibronectinA    = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
pbsWashA        = dispense 1 units of PBS_Wash
coatedChamberA  = mix fibronectinA with pbsWashA for 5m
seededChamberA  = mix cellsSeqA with coatedChamberA for 2s
heat seededChamberA at 37c for 1440m

// BB5b: First stimulus -- LPS 11 ng/mL
lps11_seqA      = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
mediaSeqA       = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
lpsMediaA       = mix lps11_seqA with mediaSeqA for 5s
seqA_firstStim  = mix seededChamberA with lpsMediaA for 120m

// BB5c: Second stimulus -- PAM 13.3 ng/mL at +2 hr
//   Delivered to the same chamber at 120 min post-LPS.
//   Chambers remain sealed; imaging continues uninterrupted.
pam13p3_seqA    = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
seqA_secondStim = mix seqA_firstStim with pam13p3_seqA for 360m

// NF-kB imaging over full 480 min window (120 + 360 min)
seqA_nfkbSignal = detect nfkbLiveImagingDetection on seqA_secondStim for 480m

// ============================================================
// BB6: seqSchemeB
// Sequential stimulation Scheme B: PAM 13.3 ng/mL delivered
// first (t=0); LPS 100 ng/mL delivered to the SAME cells
// at t=4 hr (240 min) later.
//
// Paper result (Fig. 5D): 84% of cells responded to PAM only;
// 16% responded to both. Moderate PAM stimulus activated all
// cells and induced sufficient negative feedback (A20, miR-146a)
// to fully block even a high-dose LPS response in 84% of cells.
// A20 and miR-146a mediated cross-tolerance operates across
// TLR2 and TLR4 via their shared TRAF6 downstream node.
// ============================================================

// BB6a: Cell prep for sequential scheme B
cellsSeqB       = dispense 1 units of Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
fibronectinB    = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
pbsWashB        = dispense 1 units of PBS_Wash
coatedChamberB  = mix fibronectinB with pbsWashB for 5m
seededChamberB  = mix cellsSeqB with coatedChamberB for 2s
heat seededChamberB at 37c for 1440m

// BB6b: First stimulus -- PAM 13.3 ng/mL
pam13p3_seqB    = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
mediaSeqB       = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
pamMediaB       = mix pam13p3_seqB with mediaSeqB for 5s
seqB_firstStim  = mix seededChamberB with pamMediaB for 240m

// BB6b: Second stimulus -- LPS 100 ng/mL at +4 hr
//   High-dose LPS delivered at 240 min to test whether PAM-
//   induced negative feedback blocks TLR4 cross-stimulation.
//   240 min interval chosen to ensure miR-146a is fully induced
//   (onset ~2 hr post-PAM; sustained for several hours).
lps100_seqB     = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_100ngmL
seqB_secondStim = mix seqB_firstStim with lps100_seqB for 240m

// NF-kB imaging over full 480 min window (240 + 240 min)
seqB_nfkbSignal = detect nfkbLiveImagingDetection on seqB_secondStim for 480m

// QC gate: crossToleranceDetection abstracts the dual-response
// analysis across Scheme A and Scheme B:
//   crossTolSignal > 0 encodes the expected cross-tolerance
//   outcome (majority of pre-stimulated cells refractory to
//   2nd stimulus, confirming miR-146a / A20 / IkB mechanism).
//   Representative gating on Scheme A (seqA_nfkbSignal) as
//   the primary cross-tolerance signal.
crossTolSignal  = detect crossToleranceDetection on seqA_nfkbSignal for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB7 / BB8: Cross-tolerance QC gate
// Pass (BB7): crossTolSignal > 0 -> cross-tolerance confirmed;
//             negative feedback prevents second-stimulus response
//             in the majority of pre-activated cells.
//             Dispose sequential stimulation chambers.
//             Proceed to miR-146a validation arm (BB9).
// Fail (BB8): crossTolSignal <= 0 -> no cross-tolerance;
//             cells respond to both stimuli (no NF-kB inhibition);
//             drain sequential chambers.
// Both branches converge at BB9 (crossTolJoin).
// ============================================================

if (crossTolSignal > 0) {
    dispose seqA_secondStim
    dispose seqB_secondStim
} else {
    drain seqA_secondStim
    drain seqB_secondStim
}

// ============================================================
// BB9: crossTolJoin
// Dispose sequential stimulation imaging signals and cross-
// tolerance QC signal. Control falls into miR-146a validation
// arm (BB10 / BB11).
// ============================================================

dispose seqA_nfkbSignal
dispose seqB_nfkbSignal
dispose crossTolSignal

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: miR-146a TaqMan qPCR validation
// Mechanistic validation of miR-146a as the slow, sustained
// negative feedback mediating response shutoff under low-dose
// PAM and enabling cross-tolerance.
//
// Protocol (Fig. 2C): Bulk 3T3 cells stimulated with:
//   Condition A: LPS 10 ng/mL (separate flask, not co-stim)
//   Condition B: PAM 10 ng/mL (separate flask, not co-stim)
// Time course: RNA harvested at 0, 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 hr post-stim.
// miR-146a detected by TaqMan miRNA-specific assay targeting
// hsa-miR-146a (cross-reactive with murine miR-146a).
// Normalised to snoRNA234 (snRNA endogenous control).
// Result: Both LPS and PAM induce miR-146a; LPS onset ~1 hr,
//   PAM onset ~2 hr; both maintain high expression for >6 hr.
//   Unlike IkB/A20 (return to baseline), miR-146a is sustained
//   -> ultrasensitive slow feedback (Hill coefficient 4 in model).
//
// NOTE: LPS/PAM doses for qPCR (10 ng/mL each) are intermediate
// to those used in the microfluidic experiment and represent a
// bulk cell assay condition, not the single-cell live-imaging
// doses. Separate manifests are not added for 10 ng/mL stocks
// as the qPCR uses off-chip bulk stimulation; DMEM_CompleteMedia
// and the existing LPS/PAM manifests are reused here to model
// the stimulus preparation step before cell harvest.
//
// `heat` at 37 C models the incubation period for RNA induction.
// 8 hr time course endpoint = 480 min.
// TrizolReagent: total RNA isolation (mirVana miRNA kit, Ambion).
// TaqMan_miR146a_Probe: reverse transcription + qPCR detection
//   (Applied Biosystems TaqMan microRNA reverse transcription kit
//   + TaqMan miRNA-specific assay hsa-miR-146a).
// snoRNA234_Control: endogenous control for normalisation.
// ============================================================

// Bulk stimulation for miR-146a qPCR -- LPS arm
cellsBulkLPS    = dispense 1 units of Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
mediaBulkLPS    = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
lps10_qpcr      = dispense 1 units of UltrapureLPS_11ngmL
lpsBulkStim     = mix lps10_qpcr with mediaBulkLPS for 5s
lpsQPCR_Chamber = mix cellsBulkLPS with lpsBulkStim for 480m
heat lpsQPCR_Chamber at 37c for 480m

// Bulk stimulation for miR-146a qPCR -- PAM arm
cellsBulkPAM    = dispense 1 units of Mouse3T3_p65DsRed_Cells
mediaBulkPAM    = dispense 1 units of DMEM_CompleteMedia
pam10_qpcr      = dispense 1 units of Pam3CSK4_13p3ngmL
pamBulkStim     = mix pam10_qpcr with mediaBulkPAM for 5s
pamQPCR_Chamber = mix cellsBulkPAM with pamBulkStim for 480m
heat pamQPCR_Chamber at 37c for 480m

// RNA isolation
trizolLPS       = dispense 1 units of TrizolReagent
trizolPAM       = dispense 1 units of TrizolReagent
rnaLPS          = mix lpsQPCR_Chamber with trizolLPS for 10m
rnaPAM          = mix pamQPCR_Chamber with trizolPAM for 10m

// TaqMan miR-146a detection (normalised to snoRNA234)
snoRNA_LPS      = dispense 1 units of snoRNA234_Control
snoRNA_PAM      = dispense 1 units of snoRNA234_Control
taqman_LPS      = dispense 1 units of TaqMan_miR146a_Probe
taqman_PAM      = dispense 1 units of TaqMan_miR146a_Probe

qpcrMixLPS      = mix rnaLPS with taqman_LPS for 2m
qpcrMixPAM      = mix rnaPAM with taqman_PAM for 2m

// qPCR amplification: 95 C denaturation then 60 C annealing/extension.
// Two-step TaqMan protocol; `heat` models the cycling block.
// NOTE: BioScript encodes the overall thermocycler incubation.
//   Denaturation phase modelled at 95 C for 15s (per-cycle ABI
//   TaqMan standard); extension/annealing at 60 C for 60s.
//   40-cycle qPCR total = 40 x (15 s + 60 s) = 3000 s = 50 min.
//   Encoded as two sequential heat steps per sample.
heat qpcrMixLPS at 95c for 50m
heat qpcrMixLPS at 60c for 50m
heat qpcrMixPAM at 95c for 50m
heat qpcrMixPAM at 60c for 50m

miR146a_normLPS = mix qpcrMixLPS with snoRNA_LPS for 5s
miR146a_normPAM = mix qpcrMixPAM with snoRNA_PAM for 5s

// miR-146a expression detection: signal > 0 encodes the
// expected result of sustained induction by both LPS and PAM,
// with differential onset kinetics (LPS ~1 hr, PAM ~2 hr) and
// maintained expression for the full 8-hr time course.
// Representative detection on LPS arm (primary Fig. 2C result).
miR146aSignal   = detect miR146aExpressionDetection on miR146a_normLPS for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: miR-146a QC gate
// Pass (BB10): miR146aSignal > 0 -> sustained miR-146a
//              induction confirmed; validates model slow
//              feedback mechanism; dispose qPCR samples.
// Fail (BB11): miR146aSignal <= 0 -> no miR-146a induction;
//              drain qPCR samples.
// Both branches converge at BB12 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (miR146aSignal > 0) {
    dispose miR146a_normLPS
    dispose miR146a_normPAM
} else {
    drain miR146a_normLPS
    drain miR146a_normPAM
}

// ============================================================
// BB12: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose miR146aSignal
dispose cond9a

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
